{
  "id": "ticket_01KYASA3YHA41F9TKCB0H0SHQ4",
  "name": "sessions: capture transcript on --takeover and D15 review re-entry (session ends without a snapshot)",
  "slug": "sessions-capture-transcript-on-takeover",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "sessions: capture transcript on --takeover and D15 review re-entry (session ends without a snapshot)",
    "details_md": "Discovered while fixing docs/configuration.md's transcript-capture claim (ticket housekeeping-gitignore-lock-stale): `slop start --takeover` (sessions/start.ts's buildSupersededSession) and D15's review re-entry (cli/commands/start.ts's buildReenteredSession) both end the PREVIOUS session (ended_at set) but neither calls transcript.ts's capture helper for it. stop/done/drop/review all do. The result: a session that gets forcibly superseded or re-entered never gets a transcript snapshot unless an earlier `review` call on it happened to leave one -- often exactly the sessions most worth reviewing (interrupted/handed-off work). Add best-effort capture (same 'never blocks, warns on miss' contract stop/done/drop/review already use) to both paths in src/cli/commands/start.ts before finalizing the superseded/reentered session.",
    "acceptance": [
      "slop start --takeover captures the previous session's transcript (best effort) before ending it, same warning-on-miss contract as stop/done/drop",
      "D15 review re-entry (plain slop start on a review-state ticket) captures the previous session's transcript (best effort) before ending it",
      "regression tests for both paths",
      "docs/configuration.md's Transcripts section updated again once this lands, since the gap it documents will be closed"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/cli/commands/start.ts:249 (previousSession handling, both isReviewReentry and takeover branches)",
      "src/sessions/transcript.ts (the capture helper stop/done/drop/review already use)",
      "docs/configuration.md (Transcripts section, notes this exact gap)"
    ],
    "meta": {},
    "v": 1
  },
